# Sample requests for the REST client in Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code.
# Either start PostgreSQL with `docker compose up -d postgres` and the API with `dotnet run --project src/GameOfLife.Api`,
# or start both with `docker compose up -d --build` and change baseUrl to http://localhost:8080.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5180

### Liveness: the process answers
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness: the database answers too
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Upload a vertical blinker: saved as generation 0, status Active
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cells": [
    [0, 1, 0],
    [0, 1, 0],
    [0, 1, 0]
  ]
}

### The board's current generation and status
@boardId = {{upload.response.body.$.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards/{{boardId}}

### Advance one generation and save it: the blinker turns horizontal (generation 1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards/{{boardId}}/next

### Preview ten generations after the current one, without saving
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards/{{boardId}}/ahead/10

### Jump ten generations ahead and save (generation 11)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards/{{boardId}}/ahead/10

### Find and save the final state: an oscillator with a period of 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards/{{boardId}}/final

### A settled board cannot advance: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards/{{boardId}}/next

### A rejected upload: rows of different lengths
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/boards
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cells": [
    [0, 1, 0],
    [1, 1]
  ]
}
